  "gestureRearm": {
    "note": "What a LANDED GESTURE owes the attached preview windows, and what that debt may cost in run actions. A gesture that MOVED THE DOCUMENT owes every attached window exactly one fresh evaluation; one that authored no artifact mutation owes a settled run nothing. Recording the debt is only half of paying it: a LIVE run is woken through its port, but a surface whose run has settled and been finalized holds nothing that would ask the host for another `pending_effects` poll — the host polls once per refresh and refreshes on ACTIVITY — so such a gesture carries the run start on its OWN emit (`gestureEffects`). `startLagPolls` is how many further polls the host takes before its run view reports what a request created: a request is not a state change, so an implementation that re-reads only `owed` asks again on every refresh. However long the lag, one gesture costs at most ONE `toolRunStart`, counting the one its emit carried. `runIsLive` is a link holding a job port and `runHasSettled` whether that job already reached its terminal hop: only an UNSETTLED job can be woken into more work, so a settled one leaves the gesture carrying the start itself.",
    "rows": [
      {
        "id": "a-landed-document-mutation-re-arms-one-tick-per-attached-preview",
        "windows": [
          "left",
          "right"
        ],
        "windowsSettled": true,
        "artifactMutations": 1,
        "servable": true,
        "runIsLive": false,
        "polls": 6,
        "startLagPolls": 3,
        "pollStartView": "finalized",
        "expected": {
          "owes": true,
          "owedWindows": [
            "left",
            "right"
          ],
          "hops": [
            "left",
            "right"
          ],
          "starts": 1,
          "gestureEffects": [
            "toolRunStart"
          ]
        },
        "runHasSettled": true
      },
      {
        "id": "a-gesture-that-moved-no-document-owes-the-settled-run-nothing",
        "windows": [
          "left",
          "right"
        ],
        "windowsSettled": true,
        "artifactMutations": 0,
        "servable": true,
        "runIsLive": false,
        "polls": 6,
        "startLagPolls": 3,
        "pollStartView": "finalized",
        "expected": {
